cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the original IBP model paper (Stolle et al., 2024)."
title: "IBP model — FORTRAN 77 implementation"
abstract: >-
  A portable, fixed-form FORTRAN 77 implementation of the Ionospheric Bubble
  Probability (IBP) model of Stolle et al. (2024), giving the probability of
  post-sunset equatorial plasma depletions as a function of day of year,
  longitude, local time and F10.7, using the official IBP v2.0.2 coefficients.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Safary
    family-names: Harold
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-24"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/safaryharold/ibp-fortran77"
keywords:
  - ionosphere
  - plasma bubbles
  - equatorial plasma depletions
  - IBP
  - IRI-2026
  - FORTRAN 77
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Stolle
        given-names: Claudia
      - name: "et al."
    title: "An Empirical Model of the Occurrence Rate of Low Latitude Post-Sunset Plasma Irregularities Derived From CHAMP and Swarm Magnetic Observations"
    journal: "Space Weather"
    volume: 22
    year: 2024
    doi: "10.1029/2023SW003809"
